+# Reports
+
+Every result in this directory is simulation-only. No report here describes a
+patient-data validation. Use this index to distinguish current methodology from
+archived measurements and semi-retired experiments.
+
+| file | status | provenance and scope |
+|---|---|---|
+| [`REPORT_CSD_response_derivation.md`](REPORT_CSD_response_derivation.md) | current methods reference | derives the SMI-kernel-to-MRtrix response convention used by the active manuscript simulation |
+| [`REPORT_fODF_regularization_sweep.md`](REPORT_fODF_regularization_sweep.md) | supporting measurement | synthetic parameter sweep; its preference for `lambda_nonneg = 10` is superseded by the peak-based evidence supporting the shipped default of 1 |
+| [`REPORT_fODF_outlier_cap.md`](REPORT_fODF_outlier_cap.md) | current opt-in feature | synthetic validation of the post hoc cap; a non-zero cap count on real data remains a finding to investigate |
+| [`REPORT_fODF_modulation.md`](REPORT_fODF_modulation.md) | semi-retired | modulation experiments retained for provenance; do not treat them as recommended pipeline guidance |
+| [`REPORT_SMI_deconvolution_MonteCarlo.md`](REPORT_SMI_deconvolution_MonteCarlo.md) | historical comparison | generated by the superseded campaign in [`Archive/deconv_pipeline/`](../Archive/deconv_pipeline/) |
+| [`deconv_tables.md`](deconv_tables.md) | historical generated tables | tabular output from the same superseded campaign |
+
+The active comparison is documented in
+[`deconv_comparison/README.md`](../deconv_comparison/README.md). Its manuscript
+script replaces the older cross-language campaign by running SMI, SSST-CSD, and
+MSMT-CSD on the same simulated array in one scope.
+
+When adding a report, state near the top:
+
+1. whether it is current, supporting, semi-retired, or historical;
+2. whether it uses simulation or real data;
+3. the script or workflow that generated its numbers; and
+4. whether a newer report or workflow supersedes it.
